        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The best basement crack sealer is the one that matches the crack. Leaking poured-wall cracks want polyurethane injection. Dry, structural cracks want epoxy injection after a professional opinion. Hydraulic cement is an emergency plug, caulk is for dry cracks, and coatings are for whole-wall dampness, not open cracks.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Before any of that, send roof water away from the foundation and watch the crack for a few months if you can. A sealer applied to the right crack, after the right prep, will usually outlast the house. A sealer applied to the wrong crack just moves the leak a few inches.
          </p>
